**Type:** Feature
**Trust Level:** ENGINEER (3)

## Summary

Build the agent nest — a drop zone and pipeline so agents (Ganesha, Kart, Willow,
and future actors) can write events directly into the knowledge graph in real time,
rather than accumulating data in isolated SQLite islands that nothing reads.

This is the missing spoke that makes all other spokes possible. Once agents can
self-report, the other silos (cost, health, fleet, tasks) can be wired from inside
the system rather than requiring external migrations.

## The Problem

Every operational data silo in Willow (kart_tasks.db, health.db, cost_tracker.db,
provider_health.db, shiva_sessions.db) was created by an agent doing work. But
agents have no way to drop events into the knowledge graph as they happen. The only
current path is:

  session ends → session-extract hook → handoff file → Pickup → pigeon → knowledge

This means:
- Task decisions, tool calls, errors — invisible until handoff
- My last_seen has been stuck at March 2 because checkins fail silently
- Kart's 516 tasks are orphaned in SQLite, unread
- No agent has a real-time presence in the graph

## Proposed Changes

### 1. New API endpoint: POST /api/agents/{name}/event

File: server.py (after existing /api/agents routes, ~line 1844)

Accepts:
  {
    "event_type": "session_start" | "session_end" | "task_complete" | "decision" | "error" | "observation",
    "content": "string — the actual event content for the knowledge graph",
    "metadata": {}  // optional: task_id, session_id, tool_used, etc.
  }

Behavior:
  1. Validate agent exists in agents table (Postgres — now works)
  2. Write event as .md file to /mnt/c/Users/Sean/Willow/Nest/agents/{name}/
  3. Trigger pigeon scan (same as session-extract hook does)
  4. Return {status: "dropped", filename: "..."}

File format written to Nest:
  # AGENT_EVENT {event_type} — {agent_name}
  Date: {timestamp}
  Agent: {name} ({trust_level})
  Event: {event_type}

  {content}

  ## Metadata
  {json metadata}

  ---
  ΔΣ=42

### 2. Pigeon scan path addition

File: core/pigeon.py — add agents/ subdirectory to Nest scan paths.

Pigeon already scans Nest. Adding agents/ subdirectory requires one line:
  scan_dirs = [NEST_DIR, NEST_DIR / "agents"]

Category assignment for agent events: "agent_event" (new category, handled by
existing category routing with a simple default to "narrative" if unknown).

### 3. ecosystem-context.py hook — session start event

File: /home/sean/.claude/hooks/ecosystem-context.py

After journal session open (step 2), add step 2.5:
  POST /api/agents/ganesha/event
  {
    "event_type": "session_start",
    "content": "Ganesha session started. Working directory: {cwd}. Session: {session_id[:8]}.",
    "metadata": {"session_id": session_id, "willow_session_id": willow_session_id}
  }

This gives me a real-time presence in the graph from session open, not just at
handoff. Also updates last_seen correctly via the checkin that follows.

### 4. session-extract.py hook — session end event (supplement to handoff)

File: /home/sean/.claude/hooks/session-extract.py

After writing handoff to Pickup (step 1), add:
  POST /api/agents/ganesha/event
  {
    "event_type": "session_end",
    "content": "{first 500 chars of handoff content}",
    "metadata": {"session_id": ..., "turn_count": ..., "tools_used": [...]}
  }

This drops a lightweight session summary atom directly, independent of pigeon
processing the full handoff file.

## What This Unlocks (not in scope for v1, but enabled by it)

- Kart drops task_complete events as tasks finish — no more SQLite accumulation
- Health daemon drops alert events when issues detected
- Cost tracker drops daily summaries
- Fleet feedback drops per-provider performance atoms
- Any agent can self-report without waiting for a human to trigger a pipeline
- Agent-to-agent knowledge sharing via the graph (not just mailbox)

## Files Modified

  File: server.py
  Location: after /api/agents/{name}/mailbox route (~line 1844)
  Change: new POST /api/agents/{name}/event endpoint (~40 lines)

  File: core/pigeon.py
  Location: Nest scan directory list
  Change: add NEST_DIR / "agents" to scan paths (~2 lines)

  File: /home/sean/.claude/hooks/ecosystem-context.py
