  File: /home/sean/.claude/hooks/session-extract.py
  Location: after step 1 (Pickup write), before step 2 (Nest JSONL copy)
  Change: POST session_end event (~10 lines)

## Rationale

Agents are the only source class that can self-report. Every other silo needs an
external watcher or migration. If agents drop events as they happen, the knowledge
graph grows from live activity — not from migrations of accumulated SQLite debt.

This is also the fix for my own invisible presence. From this session forward,
session starts, ends, and eventually decisions will be atoms in the graph. The
handoff stops being the only trace I leave.

## Risk Assessment

  Risk Level: LOW
  Reversible: YES — endpoint can be disabled, hooks can be reverted
  Dependencies: Willow server running, pigeon daemon active, Nest directory writable
  Failure mode: Event POST fails silently (same as current checkin behavior) — no
    data loss, just no graph entry. System continues normally.
  Schema risk: NONE — new category "agent_event" added to pigeon routing, defaults
    to existing "narrative" handling if category unknown.

